# API Patterns (Hono + Drizzle)

## Handlers

- Small, single-responsibility handlers; compose middleware for cross-cutting concerns
- Parse and validate inputs early (query, params, body)
- Return typed JSON payloads; keep shapes consistent across endpoints
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes; include error details in a safe, actionable format

## Data Access

- Keep SQL/ORM logic in small, typed functions
- Prefer parameterized queries via Drizzle; no raw string concatenation
- Map DB rows to DTOs at the boundary; avoid leaking DB schema types outward

## Errors

- Fail fast on invalid input; return 400 with message
- On unexpected exceptions, log context and return 500 with generic message

## Misc

- Read env via `process.env` with safe parsing; fail fast when required keys are missing
- When adding an external service (e.g., Spotify, Discord), expose a `verify<Service>Connection` helper
  - Run the verification during API startup alongside existing checks
  - The helper must issue a real request that validates credentials/connectivity without exhausting rate limits
  - Ensure the service route reuses shared fetch/caching logic and surfaces actionable errors in logs
